department of justice is suing the state  of texas over its new abortion law about  two dozen clinics have already stopped  abortion services omar villafranca has  been following this for us omar good  morning  good morning the doj suit puts  constitutionality at the center of the  argument now the law which is also known  as sbh bans abortion after around six  weeks which is before many women even  know they are pregnant and it makes no  exception for victims of rape sexual  abuse or incest it also puts enforcement  in the hands of citizens by allowing  anyone to sue people who help women get  an abortion like a doctor or clinical  staff or even drivers attorney general  merrick garland argues in the suit that  sba infringes on constitutional rights  and long-standing court precedent now  the supreme court recently declined to  block the law but that ruling didn't  address its constitutionality which is  what a federal judge will decide in this  suit texas governor greg abbott did  release a statement he said quote he is  confident that the courts will uphold  and protect that right to life  tony  omar thank you very much
 

